{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"stainable-crumby-chital","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nThe shipped completion-recovery design (9a08) fans out one ISOLATED evidence run per criterion after a primary-run failure. The operator has ruled this an unapproved design overreach: it explodes token cost (c9f7 shape: 22 criteria x 20-request budget = 440 requests worst case, 1.8x the primary's own 240 budget) and wall-clock cost (sequential 25-90s per criterion), re-sends the full ticket context uncached per criterion (2.67M chars for c9f7), and has no optimization for overlapping or small ACs. Meanwhile verified work from the PRIMARY run is discarded wholesale when it fails: a run that verified 20 of 22 criteria before exhausting re-does everything.\n\n## Design: bank verified ACs, resume with only the remainder\n\nReplace the per-criterion isolated fan-out with banked incremental verification:\n\n1. **Bank as you go (primary run).** Give the verifier a `record_criterion_verdict` tool: when it completes evidence for a criterion it banks {criterion_id, met, evidence, citations} immediately. Matches the convergent community pattern (incremental commit: Claude Code TodoWrite, LangGraph put_writes).\n2. **Externalized banking store.** Banked verdicts persist OUTSIDE the agent session (gate-run-scoped store keyed by ticket + base ref), so a successor run reads them without replaying the failed session.\n3. **Remainder-scoped successor.** On primary failure (runaway abort, budget/token exhaustion), spin up ONE successor run scoped to the UNVERIFIED remainder only — remaining-criteria list passed explicitly in the prompt, banked verdicts summarized read-only. Batch the remainder in a single run; do NOT fan out per criterion.\n4. **Zero-progress livelock breaker.** If a successor run banks NOTHING new, fail typed (no infinite successor chains). Community research found no prior art for this — it is our novel contribution and mandatory.\n5. **Finalizer with downgrade authority.** The tool-free finalizer assembles the verdict from banked + successor evidence. It holds explicit authority to DOWNGRADE a banked PASS on cross-criterion contradiction (banked-PASS revision is unsolved community-wide; without this, early optimistic PASSes are unrevisable). Deterministic backstop stays: an exhausted/placeholder entry can never score met=true.\n\n## Constraints (binding)\n\n- `record_criterion_verdict` must be IDEMPOTENT (double-banking on provider retry must not duplicate or corrupt) and its payload schema-versioned.\n- The finalizer receives UNCOMPRESSED per-criterion evidence — no truncation of evidence text (SWE-agent's 5000-char truncated-adjudicator hallucination failure mode).\n- Successor count is bounded (max 1 successor by default; a second only if the first banked new verdicts but still exhausted).\n- Evidence quality parity: banked evidence from the primary run must carry the same citation requirements the isolated runs enforce today.\n- The no-elision invariant holds: full ticket context byte-identical, nothing dropped (d59e).\n- Live-test on Bedrock before shipping; live tests never enter the unit suite.\n- Cache-aware prompt ordering (stable context prefix first, per-run varying material last) only after verifying our pydantic-ai runner uses the Bedrock Converse API path (legacy InvokeModel does not cache).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A primary run that verifies K of N criteria then fails leaves K banked verdicts in the externalized store, each idempotently written with evidence + citations.\n2. The successor run receives ONLY the N-K remainder as its verification scope (prompt-inspectable), plus read-only banked summaries, and runs as ONE batched run, not per-criterion fan-out.\n3. Total request spend for the c9f7 shape (22 criteria, primary verified >=15 before failing) is measurably below the current fan-out worst case: successor budget <= primary budget, never N x per-criterion budget.\n4. A successor that banks zero new verdicts raises a typed zero-progress error carrying {banked_count, remainder_count}; no third run is attempted.\n5. The finalizer can downgrade a banked PASS (unit-pinned with a contradiction fixture) and an exhausted/placeholder entry never scores met=true (deterministic backstop test).\n6. Banked evidence reaches the finalizer uncompressed (byte-identity test on evidence text).\n7. The per-criterion isolated fan-out path in completion_recovery.py is REMOVED, not left as dead code; module-size cap respected.\n8. Live Bedrock validation: one gate run on a real multi-criterion ticket demonstrating bank -> fail -> remainder successor -> finalized verdict, captured as a ticket comment.","id":"2948-48e5-666f-4677","parent_id":"10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Banked AC verification: record verified criteria incrementally, resume with remainder batch"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785991732799744001,"uuid":"4158e47d-8851-4d93-b48e-e45d52d786f1"}